"""Session 4. Words as numbers: bag of words, TF-IDF, embeddings and distance. A technical session (v3, 6 November 2026; terms and examples revised 6 November 2026;
rebuilt 11 November 2026 so that every term, symbol and formula is explained before it is used).

Teaching order (11 November 2026), one idea per slide:
a vector as a list of numbers in a fixed order (Ana rates two films (3, 4)), the same vector drawn as an arrow (direction and length), Session 2's Euclidean and Manhattan
distances recalled on the film vectors (Chloe is closer to Ana), then why direction matters, the dot product (worked, then the formula, with sigma named),
how to read a dot product (agreement, zero, the length bias), the length of an arrow (Pythagoras, square root), what an angle and its cosine mean (1, 0, -1),
cosine similarity (worked, then the formula), why cosine ignores length, the four measures compared with the working shown.
Then text: bag of words built on three tiny invented messages, cosine on those counts (filler words decide), tf and df on message M06 of the 40 messages,
idf with the natural log explained, TF-IDF worked in the textbook form tf x ln(N / df), then the smoothed form the recorded run used
(scikit-learn TfidfVectorizer defaults: idf = ln((1 + N) / (1 + df)) + 1, then each message vector divided by its length 18.54),
counts that cannot see meaning (the flood question and the force majeure clause share no word), an embedding toy with cosine, where embeddings come from,
the real 384 numbers, the demonstration and its recorded results, and why the measures agree at length 1.
The 2D map (PCA) slide was removed on 11 November 2026: PCA cannot be taught properly in the time. Its recorded numbers stay in demo_runs/.
Every recorded number comes from demo_runs/s04/ (s04_run.py, results.json) and demo_runs/s04_words_as_numbers.md.
The film ratings, the three tiny messages (S1 "send the invoice", S2 "the invoice is late", S3 "the rice is late") and the money-and-trucks toy are invented illustrations
worked by hand and checked in Python (kit/diagrams_t04.py asserts the TF-IDF numbers against results.json).
"""

